{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1ruyfsXeESiJpECw5Co", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off after filing one bug, but with low confidence (0.4) because several changed areas got only light coverage.\n\n**Bug filed:** the main screen amount editor ignores operator precedence. `518.10+5×2` showed `= $1046.2` instead of `528.1`. It evaluates left to right, so it computed (518.10+5)×2. The developer confirmed and logged it.\n\n**Checked and looked correct:**\n- **Entering expenses:** adding $5 (Food) and $3 (Transport) worked, and the daily amount updated to $1.75 after the first. A $0 amount was blocked from saving.\n- **Expense history:** the Today and 13 November sections, per-date totals, the recurring Rent entry and the \"outside of the period\" subscription view all matched the starting data. Rotating to landscape and back lost nothing.\n- **Budget sheet:** it showed $100, 11 Nov to 04 Dec, and 24 days.\n- **Categories:** adding and renaming a category worked. The category grid showed only Food and Transport, so the unused \"Gym2\" category was not saved, which I took to be expected.\n\n**Not tested:**\n- Category deletion.\n- Category icons, which the grid did not visibly show.\n- A long history scroll, which the lazy-section change targets.\n- Other arithmetic cases beyond the one precedence failure.\n\n**Data left behind:** Category list mode is still switched on in Settings → Extra features, because I turned it on to reach the category grid. The $5 Food and $3 Transport test expenses also remain."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 372, "cache_read_input_tokens": 65342, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 372}, "output_tokens": 508, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "87f5e941-8385-47e3-a59a-bcf6c92f5429", "uuid": "f8ea6836-58c2-4a88-86bc-dd98c2291819", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:18:57.510Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1ruyNGgetkdfEsfYrwA"}
